  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "# Introduction\nAs the New Main Menu releases it would be very cool to have a possibility to Use VRChat with ONLY Advanced Hand tracking.\nSystems and devices (Such as **Leap Motion** and **Vive Hand Tracking SDK**) Are able to track Complex Gestures to navigate in the Menus and to add a new dimension into avatar tracking as it could make experiences more immersive\n# Implementations\nHere are some ways Advanced Hand Tracking can be Implemented in various functions\n**Movement**\nMovement will be controlled with a virtual \"Joystick\" similar to the already existing \"One Hand Movement Menu\". There will be in the bottom right corner a small button for Jumping\nHeres an example: ![Example of One Hand Movement Menu](https://i.im.ge/2022/09/09/OvJbtq.image.png)\nThis menu will be called from the Quick Menu\n**Quick Menu, Main Menu And other Actions**\nThe Quick Menu Will be triggered by the \"Bloom\" Gesture (See Gesture List), The normal buttons will be used to Mute/Unmute. The quick menu will remain fixed like desktop Mode\nThe Action Menu will be opened by a button in the Quick menu or By the \"Circle\" Gesture. (See Gesture List)\nThe Main menu will have simple Gestures for clicking, scrolling and swiping pages, For the Main Menu movement.\n# Gestures\nHere are the Gestures that can be used for normal actions\n - \"Bloom\" Gesture, Opens and closes Quick menu. \n![Bloom Gesture](https://www.syncfusion.com/books/hololens_succinctly/Images/bloom-gesture.png)\n- \"Ready and Tap\" Gesture, Selects something in the Main menu, Quick menu and Action Menu, Also interacts with other elements (Like pressing a button In a world). Staying in the \"Ready\" Gesture will show a Laser/Pointer with smoothing to show where the Tap happens. A long tap can be used to drag sliders.\nThe \"Ready\" Gesture is the first stage of the \"Tap\" gesture. Simply Holding the Index Finger up.\n![Ready and Tap Gesture](https://docs.microsoft.com/it-it/dynamics365/mixed-reality/guides/media/air-tap-animation.gif)\n - \"Hold and Drag\" Gestures, Will be used to pick up objects. If the object has a triggerable action while picked up, Being in the \"Ready\" Gesture and using the \"Tap\" Gesture will interact with the grabbed object\n![\"Hold and Drag\" Gesture](https://i.imgur.com/yUdshke.png)\n \n - \"Swipe to left\" and \"Swipe To Right\" Gesture, Will be used to quickly swipe between Pages Of The quick menu And Main Menu.\n![Swipe To Right Gesture](https://i.imgur.com/Wqdxs5V.png)\n![Swipe To Left Gesture](https://i.imgur.com/Lb4ss4q.png)\n# Various Tracking Modes\nThere will be a total of 4 Settings for PCVR Advanced Hand Tracking and 2 Settings For Quest Hand Tracking\n**PCVR**\n 1. OFF, This will completely Turn off Advanced Hand Tracking, Using the normal Hand tracking with controllers\n 2. ON \"Leap Motion\", This option Can be toggled when a Leap motion Controller is found plugged in the Computer\n 3. ON \"Vive Hand Tracking\", This option Can be toggled when VRChat finds a PCVR Headset and the SteamVR Camera is On\n 4. Hybrid \"Leap Motion\", This option can be toggled when Leap Motion is connected. This option will only use the finger data from the Leap motion and the Hand tracking data is delivered with a controller (Or a tracker with the position of \"Right Hand\" or \"Left Hand\" in SteamVR)\n**QUEST**\n 1. OFF, This will completely Turn off Quest Hand Tracking, Using the normal Hand tracking with controllers\n 2. ON, This option can be toggled when the setting for \"Quest Hand Tracking\" is Enabled in the Quest settings.\n# Conclusion\nI Hope that This Canny Post will help A lot with the implementation of Advanced Hand Tracking with Leap Motion and Vive Hand Tracking SDK.\nThis will also help most of the sign language speakers and more Cinematic uses as well as bringing more immersion.\nDocumentations about the Vive Hand Tracking SDK can be found [Here](https://developer.vive.com/resources/vive-sense/hand-tracking-sdk/)\nDocumentations about the Leap Motion SDK can be found [Here](https://docs.ultraleap.com)\nThanks for reading!",
